      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lancing%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The area first saw settlers in the 1860s, when pioneers moved into the rugged Cumberland Plateau after the Civil War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        7,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lancing_tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lancing sits on the Cumberland Plateau at about 1,190 feet, surrounded by rolling hills and clear streams like Clear Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lancing_tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town enjoys a mild climate, averaging 54.5°F year‑round, with about 52 inches of rain and occasional snow in winter.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
